<title>HONG KONG: Siam City Cement loan raised to $81 mln.</title>
<headline>Siam City Cement loan raised to $81 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siam City Cement Public Co Ltd's term loan facility has been increased to US$81 million from US$75 million, bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The five-year loan had an average life of 3.5 years and paid a margin of 55 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate, they said.</p>
<p>Bankers said the all-in return for top-tier managers was 60 basis points, including fees.</p>
<p>NatWest Markets and Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Singapore are arrangers and joint bookrunners.</p>
<p>Twelve international financial institutions also joined the deal, bankers said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
